WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.000
Only the hard and strong may call themselves Spartans.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.000
Only the hard.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.300
Only the strong.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.000
We march.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.600
For our lands, for our families, for our freedoms.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.000
We march.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.900
Daxos! What a pleasant surprise.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.100
This morning's full of surprises, Leonidas.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.000
We've been tricked.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.200
Can't be more than a few hundred.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.800
This is a surprise.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:04.700
Silence!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.900
We heard Sparta was on the warpath,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.300
and we were eager to join forces.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.400
If it is blood you seek, you are welcome to join us.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.300
You bring only this handful of soldiers against Xerxes?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.100
I see I was wrong to expect Sparta's commitment to at least match our own.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.700
Doesn't it?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.400
You, there!

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.200
What is your profession?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.900
I'm a potter... sir.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.400
And you, Arcadian!

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.000
What is your profession?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.500
Sculptor, sir.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:43.700
You?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.200
Blacksmith.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.200
Spartans! What is your profession?!

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.600
HA-OOH! HA-OOH! HA-OOH!

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.300
You see, old friend? I brought more soldiers than you did.
